# Pages and breaks: Edges open and closed, the border and padding of a box split across pages.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Pages and breaks · Edges of a split box
	Page:
		Paper: A5
		Margin: 15mm
	Styles:
		For style: framed
			Box:
				Padding: 10
				Border: 1.5
				Border color: accent
				Background: tint
	Page overlay:
		Offset: auto 0 -24 0
		Text: Page {page} of {pages}
			Typography:
				Align: right
	Section:
		Text: Pages and breaks
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Edges of a split box
		Paragraph: A box with a border and padding that is split across pages is open at the break by default (`Edges: open`), like a sheet cut in two. With `Edges: closed`, each piece is painted as a complete box.
			Style: intro
		Block:
			Style: filler
			Box:
				Height: 280
			Text: A filler block, 280 points high, so that the next box is split between pages 1 and 2.
		Block:
			Style: framed
			Box:
				Height: 200
			Text: Edges: open
				Style: label
			Paragraph: The first piece of this box has no border or padding at the bottom.
			Paragraph: The second piece, on the next page, has none at the top.
			Paragraph: Together they read as one box cut by the page.
			Paragraph: This is the default.
		Block:
			Style: filler
			Box:
				Height: 280
				Margin: 14 0 0 0
			Text: Another filler block, so that the next box is split between pages 2 and 3.
		Block:
			Style: framed
			Box:
				Height: 200
			Break:
				Edges: closed
			Text: Edges: closed
				Style: label
			Paragraph: Each piece of this box carries its full border and padding.
			Paragraph: The piece on page 2 is closed at the bottom.
			Paragraph: The piece on page 3 is closed at the top.
			Paragraph: Each one looks like a complete box.
